tch goal, two research citations, a cross-sport analogy, and a post-match attributed quote. The writer produced only two H2 sections and omitted all of that material. A bounded rewrite against the same packet can clear all gates.","requiredRepairs":["Expand the body to at least 600 words by incorporating concrete source material the draft ignores: Pedro Porro's 58th-minute semi-final goal (named, timed) as the in-match illustration of geometry in action; Kylian MbappÃ©'s post-match attributed quote about 'a lack of communication' in France's pressing; the Phil Jackson / Chicago Bulls / Tex Winter triangle offence comparison; and the player-tracking and passing-network research cited in the source.","Add a third H2 section. The source supports distinct analytical beats â€” the probability-map framing (pitch as a map of who can reach each area first), the cross-sport comparison, and the speed-of-reconfiguration conclusion â€” that are entirely absent from the two existing sections.","Revise at least one H2 heading so that it naturally expresses the demand lens ('geometry football cup final' or a clear geometry-of-football idea). Neither 'Constructing Uncertainty' nor 'Forcing Defensive Choices' does this; the deterministic standards reading flags this as a warning.","Rewrite the ending to close on the most consequential sourced unresolved question â€” whether Argentina's preparation against Spain's triangle approach alters the geometry contest â€” using the source's own framing rather than the current vague gesture toward 'flow' and 'the trophy'.","Vary the citation pattern: 'According to [Geometry, football and the World Cup final](url)...' is a template construction in the same class the instructions limit to two appearances; the draft already risks that limit and should integrate attributions as natural prose."],"report":"**Deterministic gate status.** The standards reading records one hard error (`body-too-short`: 437 words found, 600 required) and one warning (`demand-lens-missing-h2`). The draft cannot be published in its current form.\n\n**Failure-layer diagnosis.** The earliest causal failure is the writer model, not the source material or the assignment. The primary source â€” [Geometry, football and the World Cup final](https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792) â€” is substantive. It contains Pedro Porro's 58th-minute goal as a named, timed, match-specific example; Kylian MbappÃ©'s post-match quote attributing France's collapse to \"a lack of communication\" in the press; an explained cross-sport analogy connecting Spain's triangles to the Chicago Bulls' Tex Winter triangle offence under Phil Jackson; two research citations (Nature player-tracking data, PLOS ONE passing networks); and a distinct conceptual move treating the pitch as a probability map rather than a static spatial diagram. The evidence budget the production run computes (120 licensed assertions, 600â€“850 word target) is consistent with the source's actual depth. The writer used a thin slice of that material, producing 437 words and two sections, and never touched Porro, MbappÃ©, the basketball comparison, or the research-based framing.\n\n**Claim-level audit.** Every factual claim the draft does make is supported by the witnessed source: Spain 2â€“0 France in the semi-final; the passing-triangle impression of numerical superiority; French defenders arriving a fraction too late; each pass forcing a defender to commit to one of three choices; Spain controlling when and where space would appear; triangle shape varying with ball speed, defender orientation, and available pitch area. No invented numbers, quotes, or causal mechanisms are present. The citations are syntactically adequate but patterned: \"According to [source title]...\" appears in paragraph three and approaches the template-construction limit the instructions cap at two.\n\n**Structure failures.** The draft has two H2 sections against a required three to five. Neither heading naturally expresses the search-demand lens; the deterministic warning is accurate. The ending gestures at the final as \"a laboratory for tactical reconfiguration\" without landing on any sourced, unresolved concrete question.\n\n**Fairness and harm.** No criticism of a person or institution is present; no response requirement arises. The subject is sports tactics analysis; no harm, sensationalism, or commercial-influence concern is visible.\n\n**Required path forward.** This is a bounded writer-model repair. The source packet is sufficient; no additional reporting is needed. A replay of the writer stage against the same source should incorporate the Porro goal, the MbappÃ© quote, the basketball analogy, the probability-map framing, and the passing-network research â€” bringing the draft to at least 600 words across at least three developed H2 sections, with one heading that naturally carries a geometry-of-football concept and an ending that closes on the specific open question the source raises about Argentina's preparation."}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;LBSEJMXJ79Ed8WBHNvkx_RepjDWXO6eIzNyYr_0UwrMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$98b12b09-56f2-4c44-a84b-594f63e33174ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Gxv0ZKsUNOApDg9mUQNZUOaj-qkbvHAi9_1oX_aB-ZAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhtool_useƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9l3rBliMpbzf4hVAkE2zT-88Y-UBWqXDPfs27CNCSAUƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;_YDXzolhPxLrAzvnRcJVGXpz-FvfvOqY8dnQ-OAWySQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarklwriter-modelƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;omYV3gpAaB1eI7aDd2ZiJVfHFq7pYhu4OhPaEA4bwwkƒdpairƒerightdun